---@class aws.ivs.UpdateChannelRequest
---@field arn aws.ivs.ChannelArn ARN of the channel to be updated.
---@field name? aws.ivs.ChannelName Channel name.
---@field latencyMode? aws.ivs.ChannelLatencyMode Channel latency mode. Use NORMAL to broadcast and deliver live video up to Full HD. Use LOW for near-real-time interaction with viewers.
---@field type? aws.ivs.ChannelType|string Channel type, which determines the allowable resolution and bitrate. If you exceed the allowable input resolution or bitrate, the stream probably will disconnect immediately. Default: STANDARD. For details, see Channel Types.
---@field authorized? aws.ivs.Boolean Whether the channel is private (enabled for playback authorization).
---@field recordingConfigurationArn? aws.ivs.ChannelRecordingConfigurationArn Recording-configuration ARN. A valid ARN value here both specifies the ARN and enables recording. If this is set to an empty string, recording is disabled.
---@field insecureIngest? aws.ivs.Boolean Whether the channel allows insecure RTMP and SRT ingest. Default: false.
---@field preset? aws.ivs.TranscodePreset|string Optional transcode preset for the channel. This is selectable only for ADVANCED_HD and ADVANCED_SD channel types. For those channel types, the default preset is HIGHER_BANDWIDTH_DELIVERY. For other channel types (BASIC and STANDARD), preset is the empty string ("").
---@field playbackRestrictionPolicyArn? aws.ivs.ChannelPlaybackRestrictionPolicyArn Playback-restriction-policy ARN. A valid ARN value here both specifies the ARN and enables playback restriction. If this is set to an empty string, playback restriction policy is disabled.
---@field multitrackInputConfiguration? aws.ivs.MultitrackInputConfiguration Object specifying multitrack input configuration. Default: no multitrack input configuration is specified.
---@field containerFormat? aws.ivs.ContainerFormat Indicates which content-packaging format is used (MPEG-TS or fMP4). If multitrackInputConfiguration is specified and enabled is true, then containerFormat is required and must be set to FRAGMENTED_MP4. Otherwise, containerFormat may be set to TS or FRAGMENTED_MP4. Default: TS.
---@field adConfigurationArn? aws.ivs.ChannelAdConfigurationArn ARN of the ad configuration associated with the channel.
---@field failoverSlateConfigurationArn? aws.ivs.ChannelFailoverSlateConfigurationArn Failover-slate-configuration ARN. A valid ARN value here both specifies the ARN and enables failover slate. If this is set to an empty string, failover slate configuration is disabled.

